WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.140
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.733
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:16.296
Unit seventeen: Road Safety. In this unit, you will talk about staying safe on the road.

4
00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.099
Road.

5
00:00:18.799 --> 00:00:21.762
Road means a hard way for cars and motorbikes.

6
00:00:22.062 --> 00:00:23.411
The road is busy.

7
00:00:24.111 --> 00:00:26.787
Your turn. Say: Road.

8
00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:30.163
Road.

9
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.012
Helmet.

10
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:35.640
Helmet means a hard hat that protects your head.

11
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.475
Always wear a helmet.

12
00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:41.141
Your turn. Say: Helmet.

13
00:00:43.841 --> 00:00:44.633
Helmet.

14
00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:46.931
Traffic light.

15
00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:51.767
Traffic light means red, yellow and green lights that control traffic.

16
00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.241
Wait for the green traffic light.

17
00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:58.278
Your turn. Say: Traffic light.

18
00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:02.095
Traffic light.

19
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:04.015
Cross.

20
00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:07.306
Cross means to go from one side to the other.

21
00:01:07.606 --> 00:01:09.292
Cross the road carefully.

22
00:01:09.992 --> 00:01:12.958
Your turn. Say: Cross.

23
00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:16.578
Cross.

24
00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:18.294
Look.

25
00:01:18.994 --> 00:01:21.214
Look means to use your eyes to see.

26
00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.003
Look left and right.

27
00:01:23.703 --> 00:01:26.239
Your turn. Say: Look.

28
00:01:28.939 --> 00:01:29.604
Look.

29
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:31.583
Motorbike.

30
00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:36.500
Motorbike means a vehicle with two wheels and an engine.

31
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.811
My dad drives a motorbike.

32
00:01:39.511 --> 00:01:41.827
Your turn. Say: Motorbike.

33
00:01:44.527 --> 00:01:45.528
Motorbike.

34
00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:47.506
Seatbelt.

35
00:01:48.206 --> 00:01:51.053
Seatbelt means a belt that keeps you safe in a car.

36
00:01:51.353 --> 00:01:52.900
Put on your seatbelt.

37
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.705
Your turn. Say: Seatbelt.

38
00:01:59.405 --> 00:02:00.232
Seatbelt.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:02.136
Safe.

40
00:02:02.836 --> 00:02:04.801
Safe means not in danger.

41
00:02:05.101 --> 00:02:06.973
Walking on the sidewalk is safe.

42
00:02:07.673 --> 00:02:10.616
Your turn. Say: Safe.

43
00:02:13.316 --> 00:02:14.061
Safe.

44
00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.328
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:17.628 --> 00:02:19.976
Rithy, what do you wear on a motorbike?

46
00:02:21.283 --> 00:02:22.842
I always wear a helmet.

47
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.431
Good. How do you cross the road?

48
00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:29.786
I always look left and right first.

49
00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.176
Do you cross when the light is red?

50
00:02:34.483 --> 00:02:37.449
No, never! I wait for the green light.

51
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.887
Grammar focus: Always and never.

52
00:02:42.187 --> 00:02:45.525
I always wear a helmet. I never cross without looking.

53
00:02:45.825 --> 00:02:49.603
'Always' means every time. 'Never' means not one time.

54
00:02:50.617 --> 00:02:53.513
Now read and listen. Safe on the Road.

55
00:02:53.813 --> 00:02:56.056
The roads in my town are very busy.

56
00:02:57.350 --> 00:03:00.116
I always wear a helmet on a motorbike.

57
00:03:01.417 --> 00:03:04.252
In a car, I always put on my seatbelt.

58
00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.699
Before I cross the road, I look left and right.

59
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:12.668
I never cross when the traffic light is red.

60
00:03:13.983 --> 00:03:16.752
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:17.052 --> 00:03:19.307
I blank wear a helmet on a motorbike.

62
00:03:19.607 --> 00:03:23.028
A, always. B, never. C, don't.

63
00:03:27.017 --> 00:03:29.434
The answer is A: always.

64
00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.751
A hard hat that protects your head is a blank.

65
00:03:34.051 --> 00:03:38.076
A, helmet. B, seatbelt. C, road.

66
00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.512
The answer is A: helmet.

67
00:03:46.017 --> 00:03:48.156
Wait for the blank light to cross.

68
00:03:48.456 --> 00:03:51.656
A, red. B, green. C, yellow.

69
00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.661
The answer is B: green.

70
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.079
Now it's your turn to speak. Why is a helmet important?

71
00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:13.122
A helmet is important because it protects my head. I always wear one on a motorbike.

72
00:04:13.422 --> 00:04:15.270
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:20.271
Great work today! You learned eight new words and always and never.

74
00:04:20.571 --> 00:04:25.359
Today's value is road safety. Look left and right, and wear a helmet.

75
00:04:25.659 --> 00:04:28.648
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:28.948 --> 00:04:31.485
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

